gsettings get org.gnome.settings-daemon.plugins.power sleep-inactive-ac-timeout

Put in the value in seconds. Useful for server computers that you don't want lingering around when no users are active


# Btw you can disable suspend and hibernate all together by this
https://www.tecmint.com/disable-suspend-and-hibernation-in-linux/

To disable
sudo systemctl mask sleep.target suspend.target hibernate.target hybrid-sleep.target

reboot and then query
sudo systemctl status sleep.target suspend.target hibernate.target hybrid-sleep.target

